From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:45:45 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 61/79] compute lane: an answer left inside the reopened think
 block gets the template's next turn, thinking off

With thinking on, the turn after a tool result opens a new think block. When the model wrote its answer
there and stopped at its EOS without closing the block (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next: arith-40, track-31, dp-002),
751b92d4 reported that text as the content, but it lacked the answer format the prompt asked for. The
lane now forces the template's own close after that EOS and its next assistant turn with thinking off
(read off a probe chat, so the think block closes in the template's words), and the model answers there.
The unclosed text stays reasoning. With no room for that turn, or a template without one, 751b92d4's
fallback stands.

(cherry picked from commit 969213b9c6b5ff6a3bed9ad07ab38439d3c526cd)
